    <string name="tutorial_title">TagLink Guide</string>
    <string name="tutorial_close">Got It</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_title">1. How TagLink Works</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_body">Your phone emulates an NFC Type 4 NDEF Tag. Any NFC-capable phone can tap yours and read the tag instantly without installing TagLink.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_title">2. Turn On NFC First</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_body">Device NFC must be turned on before TagLink can activate a tag. If NFC is off, use Open NFC Settings in the app or pull down your Quick Settings shade.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_title">3. Make a Tag (1 Record)</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_body">Open Make Tag, choose a single record type (URL, Wi-Fi, Contact vCard, Text, Email, Phone, SMS, Location, App, or MIME), fill the fields, and tap Write Tag. Each card stores 1 record.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_title">4. Activate &amp; Tap</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_body">Open Activate Tag, tap Activate Tag, and hold the back of your unlocked phone against the NFC reader area of the other phone for about 1 second.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_title">5. Read-Only vs Writable</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_body">Read-Only locks the virtual tag against external edits. Writable allows external NFC writing apps to overwrite the single record on your virtual card.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step6_title">6. Widgets &amp; Quick Tile</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step6_body">Use Pin a Home Screen Widget? on the home screen or Add Quick Settings Tile in Settings to toggle NFC emulation without opening the app.</string>

